# tools/bootstrap.ref: the source chain that builds the compiler.
#
# One line names each source pin, oldest first. Each line has
# `bootstrap-<n> <40-hex sha>`. The first SHA equals tools/bootstrap.seed.
# The verified user seed builds pin 0 for the selected linux or darwin target.
# Pin N builds pin N+1 for that target. The last pin builds HEAD.
#
# The SHA in this file is the fact. Historic bootstrap tags can name retired
# pins and do not select an active stage. Each pin is a repository commit. A
# shallow clone that lacks a pin cannot build. tools/pin.sh verifies the full
# SHA, ancestry, order, and numbering.
#
# Add a pin only when the prior source stage cannot build the next source. The
# cause must be an unsupported form or a source file that the next tree lacks.
# The ref change and its reason form one commit. Each pin adds one compiler
# build to both target chains, so read this rule before adding one.
bootstrap-0 6a09cbade82b87a4c36c1f67a99bd18544cc004e
